# Paths excluded from the change set under review (#105).
#
# dogfood-logs/ holds this repo's own recorded review runs. It must be ignored
# for a mechanical reason, not a cosmetic one: `check` reads the working tree as
# head, and the dogfooding convention writes each run's output.log INTO the run
# directory. The shell creates that file before the process starts, so without
# this rule the review's own log joins the diff it is reviewing, the coverage
# request key moves between the record run and the replay, and the run cannot be
# replayed at all.
dogfood-logs/

# session-state/ and docs/DEFERRED.md are working records, not deliverables:
# the rolling state of the task in flight, and the queue of things found but
# deliberately not acted on. No mandate ever asks for either, so `check`
# correctly reported them as `separable` on every single run — a caveat that
# appears unconditionally carries no information and trains the reader to skip
# the section that also holds real findings.
#
# The primary fix is that they are committed to main rather than to the branch
# under review (see CLAUDE.md). This is the backstop for when one reaches a
# branch anyway, so the review's output stays right instead of depending on the
# author having remembered.
#
# Excluding them is the same judgement `cli.py` already applies to the task
# file — "the specification, not part of the reviewed deliverable" — and not a
# way of hiding a finding: they genuinely are not part of any change under
# review. It does NOT make the tool aware it is being dogfooded; it tells the
# tool which paths are not the delivery, which is what this file is for.
/session-state/
/docs/DEFERRED.md
